# What is committed here: manifests, results, and this file. Nothing else.
#
# Replicate roots hold model-response caches worth hundreds of dollars and tens
# of megabytes of copied study data. Their PARENTS -- the promoted study roots a
# replicate freezes its options from -- are the same shape, and belong outside
# the package beside the builds they came from, in `../../replicates/`. A parent
# kept inside is either a duplicate of `data/vocabulary/` (build A's was, byte
# for byte) or a whole second study root (build B's was, 2,556 files).
#
# `!*/` is load-bearing and must stay above the file negations. Git does not
# descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so with a bare `*` the later
# `!*/manifest.json` never fires -- silently, which is how the first version of
# this file dropped every manifest while appearing to keep them.
#
# The second version said `!parents/**`, which was correct while parents/ held
# two vocabulary files and wrong the moment a full study root was created there.
# A negation whose scope is "whatever ends up in this directory" is not a rule.
# There is no parents/ rule now because there is no parents/ directory.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!/README.md
!*/manifest.json
!results/**
